C++ programming questions to practice
1. Arrays & Strings
Find the second largest element in an array without sorting.
Remove duplicates from a sorted array.
Find the missing number from 1 to N.
Find the first non-repeating character in a string.
Check whether two strings are anagrams.
Reverse a string without using reverse().
Find the longest substring without repeating characters.
Move all zeroes to the end of an array.
Find the maximum subarray sum (Kadane's algorithm).
Rotate an array by K positions.
2. Parentheses / Stack
Check whether parentheses are balanced.
Remove the outermost parentheses.
Find the next greater element.
Implement a stack using queues.
Implement a queue using stacks.
Evaluate a postfix expression.
Find the minimum element in a stack in O(1).
3. Linked Lists
Reverse a linked list.
Find the middle of a linked list.
Detect a cycle in a linked list.
Find the starting point of a cycle.
Merge two sorted linked lists.
Remove the Nth node from the end.
Check whether a linked list is a palindrome.
Find the intersection point of two linked lists.
4. Searching & Sorting
Implement binary search.
Find the first and last occurrence of an element.
Find the square root of a number using binary search.
Implement merge sort.
Implement quicksort.
Find the Kth largest/smallest element.
Search for an element in a rotated sorted array.
5. Recursion & Backtracking
Factorial and Fibonacci.
Generate all subsets of a string/array.
Generate all permutations of a string.
Solve the N-Queens problem.
Generate valid parentheses.
Solve a maze using backtracking.
6. Trees
Inorder, preorder and postorder traversal.
Level-order traversal.
Find the height of a binary tree.
Check whether two trees are identical.
Check whether a binary tree is balanced.
Find the lowest common ancestor.
Validate whether a tree is a BST.
Find the diameter of a binary tree.
